  "narrative": "No assessments are due, so I register focused refinements rather than broad residual screens. The first set tests whether the already-supported feature_003 lower-outcome pattern persists inside the exposed strata of each dominant binary predictor: feature_002=1, feature_037=1, or feature_027=1, while fixing the other dominant binary predictors and feature_063 at reference. This refines the earlier unresolved feature_003-in-exposed-subgroup signals and distinguishes whether feature_003 is an independent residual lower-outcome predictor or mainly appears in cleaned reference contexts. I anticipate a negative raw feature_003 contrast in the hypothesized direction, but plausible alternatives are attenuation or nullity because the dominant predictor may dominate the outcome surface or induce selection effects. The second set tests mutual independence of the secondary lower-outcome markers feature_003 and feature_063: feature_063=1 versus 0 within feature_003=1, and feature_003=1 versus 0 within feature_063=1, after setting feature_002, feature_010, feature_037, and feature_027 to reference. These are dataset-specific additivity tests, not mechanism claims. If lower-outcome effects saturate, the contrast inside the other exposed stratum may be attenuated; if they act along similar axes, it may be near null. The third set tests whether the feature_003 and feature_063 lower-outcome signals persist in dual nonnegative feature_018/feature_036 contexts without full conditioning on the robust binary predictors. This checks whether the accepted assay-context associations are context-independent enough to survive a simpler assay-defined stratum, or whether they depend on conditioning. Finally, I propose feature_053 high-versus-low discrete contrasts using 10 versus 2 globally and in a fully cleaned strict context, plus 5 versus 2 globally. The earlier 10-versus-5 contrast was below threshold, so a larger contrast can better bound whether feature_053 has any threshold-relevant ordinal association. All comparisons remain associations in the supplied dataset. For any valid discovery cell, I will regard the exact claim as supported only if the signed Welch lower confidence bound exceeds 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction. Cells with fewer than 20 observations will remain unresolved diagnostics, not null evidence. I also defer or close several active no-evidence screens that are lower priority than these targeted independence and assay-context refinements.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 15 explore. Validation capacity is exhausted, so registered analyses are discovery-only. Current robust axes remain feature_002 higher, feature_010 higher, feature_037 lower, and feature_027 lower. Secondary context-specific lower-outcome markers are feature_063 and feature_003. This iteration tests whether feature_003 remains a lower-outcome predictor inside exposed strata of feature_002, feature_037, and feature_027 after cleaning other dominant axes; whether feature_003 and feature_063 are mutually independent within the cleaned dominant-reference context; whether feature_003 and feature_063 lower-outcome signals persist in dual nonnegative feature_018/feature_036 contexts without full robust-flag conditioning; and whether feature_053 high-versus-low discrete contrasts have any threshold-level association. Acceptance requires signed Welch lower bound > 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction; insufficient cells remain unresolved. Lower-priority active feature_007/assay, residual binary, feature_040, and categorical screens are deferred or closed to reduce noise."
